ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS (not code dependencies)

Jev is a decision model from TypeSafe (Diogo Almeida). It is closed: no weights
and no published method. No proprietary Jev code or weights are used here. This
project derives from Kev, and makes no claim about Jev's internals.

Kev is an independent, Jev-inspired implementation by Jared Palmer. It is not
official open-source Jev. The architecture it follows was reconstructed from
external probing by Archer Hume in "Jev's Architecture Unmasked" (17 September
2026), https://archerhume.com/posts/jevs-architecture-unmasked — an inference
about Jev's internals, not confirmed knowledge of them.

Related work by the same author: ANE mutable-weight adapters,
https://github.com/MidasMulli/ane-mutable-adapters — that project hot-swaps a
LoRA adapter over a frozen resident base. THIS project is different: the adapter
is MERGED, so there are no mutable slots. See the README for why the two do not
compose today.
